FILE items/cor-the-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies-are-well-defined.md
40:## Statement
41:
42:**(a) The alephs, in ZF.** There is **exactly one** class operation
43:$\alpha \mapsto \aleph_\alpha$, defined at every ordinal ([[def-ordinal]]) and
44:given by a formula, satisfying
45:
46:$$\aleph_0 = \omega, \qquad \aleph_{\alpha + 1} = \aleph(\aleph_\alpha), \qquad \aleph_\lambda = \bigcup\{\, \aleph_\alpha : \alpha \in \lambda \,\} \ \ (\lambda \text{ a limit ordinal}),$$
47:
48:where $\aleph(\cdot)$ is the Hartogs number ([[lem-successor-cardinal-exists]])
49:and $\alpha + 1 = \alpha \cup \{\alpha\}$.
50:
51:**(b)** Every $\aleph_\alpha$ is an infinite cardinal ([[def-cardinal]]); the
52:operation is **strictly increasing**, $\alpha \in \beta \Rightarrow
53:\aleph_\alpha \in \aleph_\beta$; and it is **continuous at limits**, which is the
54:third clause read as a supremum.
55:
56:**(c)** $\alpha \le \aleph_\alpha$ for every ordinal $\alpha$.
57:
58:**(d) The beths, assuming the Axiom of Choice** ([[def-axiom-of-choice]]). There
59:is exactly one class operation $\alpha \mapsto \beth_\alpha$, defined at every
60:ordinal, with
61:
62:$$\beth_0 = \omega, \qquad \beth_{\alpha + 1} = 2^{\beth_\alpha}, \qquad \beth_\lambda = \bigcup\{\, \beth_\alpha : \alpha \in \lambda \,\} \ \ (\lambda \text{ a limit ordinal}),$$
63:
64:and it too takes infinite cardinal values, is strictly increasing, and is
65:continuous at limits.
66:
67:Like [[lem-recursion-on-the-ordinals]] these are **theorem schemas**: an instance
68:for each of the defining formulas. The aleph half uses Replacement and no choice; the
69:beth half needs the Axiom of Choice, and needs it only because $2^{\kappa}$ does
70:([[thm-cardinal-power-set-and-cantor]]).
71:
