items/thm-kuratowski-closure-axioms.md:111:- **(K3) is what makes $c$ recoverable as the closure operator of its fixed-point topology.** Dropping it leaves an operator whose fixed points still satisfy (C1), (C2) and (C3) — steps 1.3, 1.4 and 2.1 do not use it — but the closure operator of the resulting topology is then only the smallest fixed point above $A$, which need not be $c(A)$. It is step 4.1 that spends (K3).
